*************************************************************************
* Data selection for Secondary outcome: Positive predictive values (PPV)*
*************************************************************************

//This do-file is intended for calculating the secondary outcomes (the ones possible to calculate based on the extracted false positive data). First, I will call the cleansed dataset and then pick out only the variables I need. Then, I will calculate positive predictive values and their standard errors. Last, I will calculate the relative risks of PPVs.

clear

* Set working directoryCalling
cd "C:\Users\wpoulsen\OneDrive - Syddansk Universitet\PhD\SR MA false screening results\Statawork\FP outcomes\data\PPV"
* Calling the cleansed dataset and keeping only the variables I need for calculating the secondary outcome (numbers of false positives and numbers of true positives)
use "C:\Users\wpoulsen\OneDrive - Syddansk Universitet\PhD\SR MA false screening results\Statawork\Final files first and updated search\FPdatasetCleansed"
keep study_number author publication_year design gfobt_fit type cutoff def_true_positive population num_participants screening_round exp_ref_comp num_ref num_comp num_FP_ref num_FP_comp num_TP_ref num_TP_comp rob final_decision popu
label variable publication_year "Year"
label variable num_FP_ref "FP_ref"
label variable num_TP_ref "TP_ref"
label variable num_FP_comp "FP_comp"
label variable num_TP_comp "TP_comp"

* Keeping only the comparisons where the relevant metrics are available
keep if final_decision=="Resolved" | final_decision=="Resolved. Only include in PPV analysis. Do not use for specificity" //Final_decision "Resolved" means that the study is eligible based on our protocol criteria. "Resolved, only include in PPV analysis. Do not use for specificity" means that FN are not available and it cannot be used in the FN part of the study. But in the FP part it can.
drop if exp_ref_comp=="Age (means compared)" | exp_ref_comp=="Age at screening (as a continious variable)" //Dropping exposures that are declared as resolved and thus eligible, but where numbers are presented as continous variable. Thus it is not possible to use in binary comparisons.
drop if num_FP_ref==. | num_FP_comp==. | num_TP_ref==. | num_TP_comp==. //Dropping comparisons where numbers of FP or TP are not available

* Inspecting and sorting the dataset
sort author publication_year
table exp_ref_comp if gfobt_fit=="FIT" //showing exposures available for calculations for studies testing with FIT
table exp_ref_comp if gfobt_fit=="gFOBT" // showing exposures available for calculations for studies testing with gFOBT
table exp_ref_comp if gfobt_fit=="gFOBT and FIT" // showing exposures available for calculations for studies testing with a combination of gFOBT and FIT

* Calculate outcomes
* Positive predictive values for reference and comparison groups, respectively. These numbers are what is needed to go in the numerator and denominator. Generate log-transformed RR of FPR to be used in funnel plots. And calculate standard errors (s.e.(logRR))
gen PPV_ref = num_TP_ref/(num_TP_ref+num_FP_ref)
label variable PPV_ref "Positive predictive value for reference group"
gen PPV_comp = num_TP_comp/(num_TP_comp+num_FP_comp)
label variable PPV_comp "Positive predictive value for comparison group"
*Then calculate RR of PPVs with comparison group in numerator. And generate log-transformed RR of FPR to be used in funnel plots.
gen RR_PPV_comp_ref = PPV_comp/PPV_ref
label variable RR_PPV_comp_ref "Relative risk of positive predictive values in comparison group versus reference group" //be aware of missing values due to 0 observations in some cells
gen log_RR_PPV_comp_ref = log(RR_PPV_comp_ref)
label variable log_RR_PPV_comp_ref "log-transformed relative risk of positive predictive values in comparison group versus reference group"
gen se = sqrt(1/num_TP_comp-1/(num_TP_comp+num_FP_comp)+1/num_TP_ref-1/(num_TP_ref+num_FP_ref)) //be aware of missing values due to 0 observations in some cells
label variable se "Standard Error for logRR"

* Generate variable with sums of participants contributing to calculations of PPVs. This will be needed when prioritizing largest populations in situations where data from several screening rounds is available to get the most robust estimates. (We have extracted data on total numbers in comparison and references groups, but in some cases this number is divided between TP-FP-FN-TN, of which two of the measures are not part of the PPV calculations. Hence, we generate a new variable counting only the participants included in the PPV calculations.)

gen total_part = num_TP_ref+num_FP_ref+num_TP_comp+num_FP_comp

* Generate author, year variable for Forest plots
gen author_year = author + ", " + string(publication_year)

* Generate risk factor variable for tables
gen str100 rf = ""

* Preserving dataset
preserve

***********************************
* Starting data selection with exposures available from studies mixing the use of FIT and gFOBT
***********************************
* Sex (female vs. male)
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data mixing gFOBT and FIT is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Sex"))
replace rf = "Sex"
save "ppv_gfobtfit_sex.dta", replace
restore

* Age 50-59 vs. 60-69 (one study 50-60 vs. 60-69)
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data mixing gFOBT and FIT is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "50-59")) | (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "50-60"))
keep if (strpos(population, "prevalent")) //keeping only data from prevalent round in study where data from both prevalent and incident rounds are available
replace author_year = "SalasTrejo, 2017, males" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age in men (50-59 vs. 60-69)"))>0
replace author_year = "SalasTrejo, 2017, females" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age in women (50-59 vs. 60-69)"))>0
replace rf = "Age (50-59 vs. 60-69)"
save "ppv_gfobtfit_age50-59vs60-69.dta", replace
restore

***********************************
* Continuing with exposures available from studies using only gFOBT
***********************************
* BMI <25 vs. 25-29.9
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "BMI (<25 vs. 25-29.9)"))
replace rf = "BMI (<25 vs. 25-29.9)"
save "ppv_gfobt_bmibel25vs25-30.dta", replace
restore

* BMI <25 vs. >=30
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "BMI (<25 vs. ≥30)"))
replace rf = "BMI (<25 vs. ≥30)"
save "ppv_gfobt_bmibel25vsab30.dta", replace
restore

* Sex (female vs. male)
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Sex"))
drop if study_number==5 & (strpos(population, "incident")) //dropping repeat populations from the same study while keeping the round with the largest population
drop if study_number==97 & (strpos(population, "prevalent")) //dropping repeat populations from the same study while keeping the round with the largest population
drop if study_number==40 & (strpos(population, "prevalent")) //dropping repeat populations from the same study while keeping the round with the largest population
drop if study_number==37 //dropping a study by Steinmetz due to risk of overlapping populations in another study by the same author
replace author_year = "Mooers, 2018, female 50-54 vs. male 50-54" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Sex in age groups at time of endoscopy (female 50-54 vs. male 50-54)"))>0
replace author_year = "Mooers, 2018, female 60-64 vs. male 60-64" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Sex in age groups at time of endoscopy (female 60-64 vs. male 60-64)"))>0
replace author_year = "Mooers, 2018, female 70-75 vs. male 70-75" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Sex in age groups at time of endoscopy (female 70-75 vs. male 70-75)"))>0
replace author_year = "Mooers, 2018, female 55-59 vs. male 55-59" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Sex in age groups at time of endoscopy (female 55-59 vs. male 55-59)"))>0
replace author_year = "Mooers, 2018, female 65-69 vs. male 65-69" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Sex in age groups at time of endoscopy (female 65-69 vs. male 65-69)"))>0
replace rf = "Sex"
save "ppv_gfobt_sex.dta", replace
restore

* Age (50-54 vs. 55-59) (one study grouping 50-55 vs. 56-60)
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age"))
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age (50-54 vs. 55-59")) | (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age (50-55 vs. 56-60)"))
drop if study_number==40 & (strpos(population, "prevalent")) //dropping repeat populations from the same study while keeping the round with the largest population
replace rf = "Age (50-54 vs. 55-59)"
save "ppv_gfobt_age50-54vs55-59", replace
restore

* Age (50-54 vs. 60-64) (one study grouping (50-55 vs. 61-65))
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age"))
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age (50-54 vs. 60-64)")) | (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age (50-55 vs. 61-65)"))
drop if study_number==40 & (strpos(population, "prevalent")) //dropping repeat populations from the same study while keeping the round with the largest population
replace rf = "Age (50-54 vs. 60-64)"
save "ppv_gfobt_age50-54vs60-64", replace
restore

* Age (50-54 vs. 65-69) (one study grouping 50-55 vs. 66-70)
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age"))
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age (50-54 vs. 65-69)")) | (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age (50-55 vs. 66-70)"))
drop if study_number==40 & (strpos(population, "prevalent")) //dropping repeat populations from the same study while keeping the round with the largest population
replace rf = "Age (50-54 vs. 65-69)"
save "ppv_gfobt_age50-54vs65-69", replace
restore

* Age (50-54 vs. 70-74) (one study grouping 50-55 vs. 71-75)
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age"))
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age (50-54 vs. 70-74)")) | (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age (50-55 vs. 71-75)"))
replace rf = "Age (50-54 vs. 70-74)"
save "ppv_gfobt_age50-54vs70-74", replace
restore

* Age (55-59 vs. 60-64)
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age"))
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age at colonoscopy"))
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "(55-59 vs. 60-64)"))
replace author_year = "Brenner, 2014, males" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age at colonoscopy in men (55-59 vs. 60-64)"))>0
replace author_year = "Brenner, 2014, females" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age at colonoscopy in women (55-59 vs. 60-64)"))>0
replace rf = "Age (55-59 vs. 60-64)"
save "ppv_gfobt_age55-59vs60-64", replace
restore

* Age (55-59 vs. 65-69)
preserve
keep if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT"))
drop if (strpos(gfobt_fit, "gFOBT and FIT"))
codebook gfobt_fit //ensure that only data from gFOBT only is left
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age"))
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age at colonoscopy"))
keep if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "(55-59 vs. 65-69)"))
replace author_year = "Brenner, 2014, males" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age at colonoscopy in men (55-59 vs. 65-69)"))>0
replace author_year = "Brenner, 2014, females" if (strpos(exp_ref_comp, "Age at colonoscopy in women (55-59 vs. 65-69)"))>0
